    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "History",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Trinity Congregational Church began in a house on Brixton Hill soon after St. Matthew’s Church was built.  In 1828 these dissenters began to build a chapel, on what is now St. Matthew’s Road, taking on a debt which took many years to pay off. The church has always been financed by members and friends. There have been a few changes to the chapel since 1828, including the installation of a Bevington organ.  A new, larger chapel was planned at the beginning of the 20th century, but this never came to fruition.\nThe church has minute books from the past, magazines prepared by the young men before World War 1 and literature about its history."
            ]
        }
